module nupp.mem

--[[
`nupp.mem` groups storage allocators with different lifetime contracts.
Checked views make their elements safe to index.

Nothing is re-exported here: every member is a module of its own, reached by the
name it has.

```nupp
const span = binary.span

local struct Point
    x: number
    y: number
end

const storage = carray(Point, 4)
const points = span.fromcarray(storage, 4)

print(points[1].x)
```

[](binary.span) provides rooted shared and writable views used by arrays and
structure-of-arrays storage. Element positions are one-based, and indexing and
slicing check the view's element count.

Managed arrays and arena pages remain live through references to their storage.
Heap and SoA allocations return affine owners with lexical cleanup. Immutable
shared-byte regions retain engine-owned blocks and require the Nupp engine
host. See each module's API for its allocation and lifetime contract.

Record-backed pooling is [](table.Pool). Struct rows use [](nupp.mem.arena),
whose release ends a lease and whose reset rewinds the allocation cursor.

See [c-interop.md](docs/learn/runtime/c-interop/index.md) for what crossing the
C boundary costs, and
[ownership.md](docs/learn/runtime/ownership/borrowing.md) for the borrow rules
these views are written against.
]]
